   "wasmSdk": "swift-6.2-RELEASE_wasm.artifactbundle.tar.gz sha256 fe4e8648309fce86ea522e9e0d1dc48e82df6ba6e5743dbf0c53db8429fb5224 (swift.org release 6.2, Wasm SDK; no wasm SDK exists for 6.1.x)",
   "wasmtime": "50.0.0",
   "node": "26.5.0",
   "nativeFlags": "swiftc -O (the matrix build line, dynamic stdlib)",
   "wasmFlags": "swiftc -O -target wasm32-unknown-wasip1 -sdk WASI.sdk -resource-dir swift_static -static-stdlib -Xclang-linker -resource-dir -Xclang-linker swift_static/clang -Xlinker -z -Xlinker stack-size=8388608"
  },
  "transforms": [
   "int64.sh (languages/wasm/swift/int64.sh + int64-shim.swift), wasm build of 11 benchmarks only (dijkstra gbdt gemm k-means lz77 polymorphism reverse-complement sha256 sort-search viterbi vm): inserts after `import Foundation` typealiases making untyped integer literals, Int and UInt 64-bit, plus Array Int64 subscript/init/reserveCapacity overloads. Needed because Swift's Int is 32 bits on wasm32. Measured natively by the native-shim column: identical on 9 of the 11, dijkstra +0.88%, sha256 +0.098%. The other 7 benchmarks are built from the unmodified canonical source."
  ],
  "asymmetries": [
   "Swift version: the matrix is 6.1.3 but the first official wasm SDK is 6.2; native and wasm both use 6.2.0 here, so the native column is not the matrix Swift cell",
   "wasm links the stdlib and Foundation statically (-static-stdlib, from the SDK toolset); native links them dynamically, as in the matrix. Startup cancels in the differential",
   "wasm32 Int is 32 bits: the 11 shimmed benchmarks run with Int64 (emulating the native 64-bit Int); array indexing then truncates an Int64 to the 32-bit address index, an extra wrap that native does not have. The other 7 run with the real 32-bit Int on wasm and 64-bit Int natively",
   "wasm shadow stack raised to 8 MiB (SDK default 64 KiB) to match the native 8 MiB main-thread stack",
   "wasm32-wasip1 libc is wasi-libc (dlmalloc) with Swift's wasm runtime; native uses glibc malloc",
   "no -swift-sdk option in swiftc 6.2: the SDK is wired by hand with -sdk/-resource-dir/-static-stdlib exactly as its swift-sdk.json and toolset.json specify",
   "the native column is aarch64 machine code, so ratios mix ISA with wasm cost; native is run under the gcc:14/trixie base (not the matrix swift image) with swift runtime libs copied to /opt/swift-rt",
   "the Int64 shim is not a perfect no-op natively: the native-shim column matches the unmodified native build exactly on 9 of the 11 shimmed benchmarks, dijkstra is +0.88% and sha256 +0.098%"
  ],
